The file is written and validated. Summary of the design decisions:

| Requirement | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Enterprise edition, org `Contoso Service` | `edition: "enterprise"`, `orgName` |
| Service Cloud user licence (admin) | `features: ["EnableS1Desktop"]` — this feature enables Service Cloud and grants the admin the Service Cloud licence |
| Lightning Knowledge (not Classic) | `lightningExperienceSettings.enableLightning: true` (Lightning client) + `knowledgeSettings.enableKnowledge: true` |
| Omni-Channel enabled | `serviceSettings.enableOmniChannel: true` (plus `enableWork`, `enableRouting`, `enableCaseRouting` — all documented `ServiceSettings` fields) |
| Lightning Service Console licence (admin) | **Left out** — no def-file element exists for named user licences; a post-create script assigns it |
| Skills-based routing | **Left out** — skills, service channels and routing configs ship with the source deployment; there's no def-file flag |

Only schema-valid fields are included, so `sf org create scratch` won't fail on unknown elements on the current release.

